<!--
  T09 Array and Path

  AN ARRAY ROW AND A DOTTED PATH. [double] is a shape, not a quantity, so it
  carries no unit; a row whose of= names another model's row is drawn as a
  reference and must resolve.

  A UNIT TEST DESIGN. Bundled with the app and read-only: suite [25]
  asserts what this file is supposed to prove, so editing it here
  changes what the harness tests.
-->
<gorp name="T09 Array and Path">
  <!-- nos-uml-state {"mode":"ai-design","title":"T09 Array and Path","layout":{"ut.path.Series":{"x":60,"y":60,"w":280,"h":140},"ut.path.Window":{"x":60,"y":280,"w":280,"h":140},"ut.path.Smooth":{"x":440,"y":160,"w":280,"h":140},"ut.path.Smoothed":{"x":800,"y":160,"w":280,"h":140}}} -->

  <comment view="class">An array row and a dotted path. values : [double] is a SHAPE, not a quantity, so it carries no unit and needs no collapse. Window.source is a key whose of= names another model's ROW — ut.path.Series.id — and the reference arrow is anchored on that row.

A dotted path must resolve to something that exists; longest-prefix resolution is what finds Series from Series.id.</comment>
  <expect>Check finds nothing: the array rows are exempt from the measurement rule and the path resolves.

Point source at a row that does not exist and Check must say so, naming Window.source.</expect>
  <model namespace="ut.path.Series">
    <variables>
      <variable name="id"     type="key" />
      <variable name="values" type="[double]" />
    </variables>
  </model>

  <model namespace="ut.path.Window">
    <variables>
      <variable name="source" type="key" of="ut.path.Series.id" />
      <variable name="width"  type="int" collapse="Sum"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
    </variables>
  </model>

  <algorithm namespace="ut.path.Smooth">
    <input  model="ut.path.Window" />
    <output model="ut.path.Smoothed" />
    <operations>
      <operation name="smooth" returns="[double]" />
    </operations>
  </algorithm>

  <model namespace="ut.path.Smoothed">
    <variables>
      <variable name="values" type="[double]" />
    </variables>
  </model>
</gorp>
